+# Pre-registration 01 — spn117: the shadow spine of route A, stage 4 part 1 (K5 reproduction, K1 price)
+
+Session 117. ROADMAP §0.1 "СЕССИЯ 117 — ЗАПИСИ ДО ДЕЙСТВИЙ" items 3–11 (item 11: the pre-seal check and its fixes);
+design `docs/session-117/designA4_spine.md`.
+Sealed before the run; not edited after it (the scorer checks this file's sha256 against the one `enter_scene.py`
+records before the emulator starts).
+
+## What runs
+
+- Build `3cde1af8ed1af960a2216957288c6d9f54e606fd7c3e48bd97659b052a9c64b9` (git `36c8350`: `spine` knob, 0..2, default
+  0, measurement only; `operator== = default` on the 61 register types of `hardwareContext.h`; nothing under
+  `src/graphics/shader/**`). Its embedded label reads `…-gfbcfd49-dirty`: it was built from the working tree a second
+  before commit `36c8350`, whose only source change over `fbcfd49` is the `graphicsRun.cpp` fix it contains. Pinned copy
+  `C:/kyty/s117/kyty_emulator_3cde1af8.exe`, installed by the chain.
+- Chain `go117a.sh spn117`: Sky Garden, one attempt, 300-s hold, `KYTY_GPU_CLOCK_PIN=1`, `KYTY_GPU_MARKERS=0`, no video,
+  gates `gates_base.txt`, schedule `KYTY_GATE_SCHEDULE=90+1800:spine=1|spine=2` with `KYTY_GATE_SCHEDULE_ABBA=1`. The chain
+  refuses while the lock is held, any process is busy (> 0.5 CPU s/s), any `mutlib.py` process lives, or CPU ≥ 15 % /
+  GPU ≥ 10 %.
+- Scorer `spn117.py` (its docstring is the full rule set; fixtures `test_spn117.py`; mutants `mut_spn117.py`, run through
+  the frozen `mutlib` v4.1 `--control --no-memo` on the sealed copy, tally appended to `SEALS117.txt` before the run).
+
+## Admission (NOT_ADMITTED unless every one holds)
+
+Build and installed exe; pin (env and exactly one `GpuClockPin: mode 1`); the exact `KYTY_*` environment (with the
+schedule and ABBA) and only `VK_SDK_PATH` of `VK_*`; hold 300 s; exactly one attempt, ok, no hold exit; this
+pre-registration (path and sha256); the gate text of `gates_base.txt` without a `spine=` token; every `Gate:` line is the
+schedule's own flip of `spine` at a block start with the value of that block's arm; every `GateArm:` line well-formed,
+2 arms, period 90, ABBA flag 1, arm texts `spine=1` / `spine=2`, block `b` at frame 1800 + 90·b, arm order A B B A;
+exactly one `Spine: mode=` line; no failure marker (`GpuHangAbort`, `GpuWaitSlow`, `GpuMarkerHung`, `GpuCheckpointHang`,
+`ErrorDeviceLost`, `std::terminate`, `abort()`, `fatal`, `Unhandled exception`, `--- Error ---`,
+`AsyncPipelines: skipped draw`) in the log or stdout; ≥ 20 complete blocks of each arm; armed (arm 0 plans and never
+compares on at most 1 % of its elements on kept frames, arm 1 compares); `el_ops`: `spine_el` / (draws + dispatches)
+over the kept frames of arm 1 within [0,95; 1,05]; GPU idle before the run (median ≤ 10 %).
+
+## Verdicts (fixed now)
+
+- **K5 (reproduction)** over every `FrameTrace-x` line after frame 1800 (duplicates and frames missing other lines
+  included): **FAIL** if any `spine_bad`, `spine_misal` (a submission's real element count differs from its plan) or
+  `cram_write` (const RAM is outside the compare), or any `SpineMismatch:` / `SpineMisalign:` line in the log; **PASS**
+  if none and `spine_cmp` ≥ 90 % of `spine_el` over the kept frames (10–89) of arm-1 blocks; else **NOT_EVALUABLE**.
+  `spine_pad` (bytes differ only in padding), `spine_lost` (compares lost because another plan of the same processor
+  replaced the snapshots — an instrument limit, caught by the ratio) and `spine_abort` are reported, not failing.
+- **K1 (price):** mean `spine_ns`/1000 over the kept frames of arm-0 blocks ≤ **1 200 µs** ⇒ PASS; else FAIL, and then
+  **walker fit** = mean(`da_walk_us` + `spine_ns`/1000) < mean(`dt_us` − `spine_ns`/1000) over the same frames (the
+  frame the GuestGpu thread would have without the spine; the first draft compared with `dt_us`, which the spine itself
+  lengthens, and could never fail).
+
+## Consequences (fixed now, ROADMAP 117 item 4)
+
+| outcome | consequence |
+|---|---|
+| NOT_ADMITTED | one repeat `go117a.sh spn117r`; a second NOT_ADMITTED ⇒ stage 4 is recorded as not measured and the next step is decided in ROADMAP before any action |
+| K5 FAIL | **STOP_STAGE4**: route A stops at stage 4 until the hazard the `SpineMismatch:` / `SpineMisalign:` lines name has a design, recorded before any code |
+| K5 NOT_EVALUABLE | one repeat `spn117r`, after the cause (aborts / lost compares) is recorded |
+| K5 PASS, K1 PASS | **PART2**: stage 4 part 2 (K3 pass histogram, K4 image overlap of adjacent segments), batched per item 6 |
+| K5 PASS, K1 FAIL, walker fit | **PART2_WALKER**: part 2, with the spine planned on the `dawalk` walker thread |
+| K5 PASS, K1 FAIL, no walker fit | **CLOSE_A**: route A closed for maximum FPS |
+
+Nothing ships from this seal; the `spine` knob stays default 0 whatever the outcome.
+
+## Before the seal (disclosed)
+
+Three UNSEALED smoke runs of the instrument (ROADMAP 117 items 8–10; Sky Garden 120 s, `spine=2` from the gate file, no
+pin, no schedule; their numbers decide nothing): `smoke117` (build `af50e1b4`) and `smoke117b` (`175936c8`) found two
+spine defects — the dispatch's own wave-size write and the `R_DISPATCH_RESET` processor reset, both fixed in code before
+this build — and `smoke117c` on THIS build read 0 `spine_bad` in 19.7 M compares, 0 aborts / misaligns / lost compares,
+`spine_ns` ≈ 0.84 ms a frame (mode 2, unpinned). So this seal is expected to PASS both K5 and K1; it exists to confirm
+that on the pinned, scheduled run with both modes, and to price mode 1 alone. The verdict rules and consequences above
+were recorded in ROADMAP items 4–5 before any smoke run.
+
+## Predictions (report only, not verdicts)
+
+`spine_ns` 200–1 500 µs a frame (the walker's partial decode `da_walk_us − da_queue_us` was 1 085 µs in session 104);
+`spine_el` within 5 % of draws + dispatches minus predicated skips; `spine_pad` 0 or small (smoke read 0); `spine_bad` 0 is the hypothesis under test, with the most likely failure the GPU-dependent
+words (`SET_PREDICATION` with wait, `COND_EXEC`) read at plan time.
+
+## Limits
+
+One entry, one launch state (BDA regime not relevant to the spine, reported by nothing here); mode 2 costs
+milliseconds a frame (snapshots 4 096 B an element: `HW::Context` 2 672, `HW::UserConfig` 148, `HW::Shader` 1 208, as `Spine:` logs), so arm-1 levels are not speed levels; the spine is seeded from the
+real state at every submission start, so it proves reproduction within a submission, not the carry across submissions;
+`m_num_instances` (rewritten by indirect draws from GPU-written arguments) and const RAM are not compared (const RAM
+writes are counted by `cram_write`); `float` register fields holding NaN would read as `spine_bad`; the words the plan
+reads early (predication, `COND_EXEC`, the 14-dword branch) were never met in Sky Garden in the smoke runs.
